  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3221.04 Bumpers",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3221.04 Bumpers.\n\n(a) A vehicle shall be rejected if the bumper and its structural components are:\n\n(1) Not attached to the front and rear of a passenger or multipurpose vehicle as manufacturer intended;\n\n(2) Not attached to the front and rear of a pick-up truck as manufacturer intended;\n\n(3) Located at an improper height as measured pursuant to RSA 266:9;\n\n(4) Loose or improperly installed; or\n\n(5) Rusted so that it is not firmly attached or that has broken or torn portions protruding from the surface so as to create a hazard; or\n\n(6) Damaged to a degree which does not effectively reduce the transfer of impact when engaged.\n\n(b) Any vehicle equipped with a tow trailer hitch shall be rejected if it does not have a solid structural integrity and is not securely mounted to the vehicle frame.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16; amd by #12932, eff 11-27-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
